data: {"items":[{"panelist":"margo-brandt","claim":"quoted lead times in the fifty-to-seventy-week range","tag_given":"SRC","tag_should_be":"EST","note":"The survey reports vendor self-declared lead times; vendor projections are at most EST, never SRC."},{"panelist":"albert-thorne","claim":"flat profiles have been moving up the queue in recent large-load orders","tag_given":"EST","tag_should_be":"INF","note":"No retrieved artifact supports the queue-position claim; without a second source it is inference."}],"verdicts":{"margo-brandt":"One downgrade: vendor lead times are EST, not SRC. Sequence stands. Proceed.","mach-eigen":"Busbar amperage is EST with the method stated; the shelf envelope is SRC to the rack standard. Clean. Proceed.","delia-marchetti":"All framing claims correctly tagged INF; the backlog citation is SRC. Proceed.","albert-thorne":"One downgrade: the queue-position claim is INF without a second feed. Study timeline is SRC. Proceed.","hartford-nakamura":"Every exposure claim tagged INF as it should be. Nothing to strike. Proceed.","rosalind-ferraro":"Backlog citation is SRC; the rest is correctly INF. Proceed.","victoria-stroud":"Basis-point range is EST with a stated basis; the prior ruling is SRC, correctly not VRF. Proceed.","ingrid-halverson":"Thermal gain is EST; the shelf envelope is SRC. Units present throughout. Proceed."}}

